Subject: Diagnostic: the audio plays on through rollbacks, in a heap of its own
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Rollback study, after tweak patch 0029. The audio plays on through
rollbacks: its state lives in a heap of its own, which no rollback restores.
The functions the game calls into the audio (the 45 the rest of the module
uses, the audio system's creation in main, and the callbacks the audio hands
the AX, alarms, the pads, disc reads and its bundles' loading) enter and
leave it, and inside it AllocateMemory takes the port's audio allocator. A
replayed frame starts, stops, pauses and resumes no sound: it did when it
first ran. The audio's streams read the disc while rollbacks happen:
mscharged_rollback_async_read_state returns the disc reads' manager, which
the port leaves out of the rollback.

Add include/mscharged_rollback_audio.h, its interface to the port.

Without RECHARGED_ROLLBACK_TEST or RECHARGED_ROLLBACK nothing changes.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_rollback_audio.h b/include/mscharged_rollback_audio.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7e5da7b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/mscharged_rollback_audio.h
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+#ifndef MSCHARGED_ROLLBACK_AUDIO_H
+#define MSCHARGED_ROLLBACK_AUDIO_H
+
+// The audio under the rollback (the port's src/platform/rollback_audio.cpp):
+// its state lives in a heap of its own, which no rollback restores, as the
+// sound it describes goes on.
+#include "mscharged_rollback.h"
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+// The functions the game calls into the audio enter and leave it
+// (MSCHARGED_AUDIO_SCOPE); inside, mscharged_rollback_audio_allocator is the
+// allocator every allocation uses, null outside or without the rollback.
+void mscharged_rollback_audio_enter(void);
+void mscharged_rollback_audio_leave(void);
+void* mscharged_rollback_audio_allocator(void);
+// The game's: the disc reads' manager and its tail buffers, which go on
+// whatever the match does (a rollback must not take back a read under way,
+// as the audio's streams have); returns how many pointers, at most capacity.
+int mscharged_rollback_async_read_state(const void** pointers, int capacity);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+
+struct MschargedAudioScope
+{
+    MschargedAudioScope() { mscharged_rollback_audio_enter(); }
+    ~MschargedAudioScope() { mscharged_rollback_audio_leave(); }
+};
+// At the start of an audio function the game calls: its allocations go to the
+// audio's heap.
+#define MSCHARGED_AUDIO_SCOPE() MschargedAudioScope mschargedAudioScope
+// At the start of one that starts, stops, pauses or resumes sound: a replayed
+// frame does nothing (it did it when it first ran) and returns the value given.
+#define MSCHARGED_AUDIO_ACTION(...)                                                                  \
+    if (mscharged_rollback_resimulating()) return __VA_ARGS__;                                       \
+    MSCHARGED_AUDIO_SCOPE()
+
+#endif
+
+#endif // MSCHARGED_ROLLBACK_AUDIO_H
+#endif // MSCHARGED_TWEAKS
